(a) total quantity and value of rice dispatched from warehouses of FCI to Ethanol plants during the last 12 months up to June, 2026, State-wise;
(b) average price per quintal at which such Rice is sold to Ethanol plants vis-a-vis average cost of procurement;
(c) whether any subsidy is being extended to Ethanol producers for procurement of Rice supplied for Ethanol production, if so, total amount of subsidy provided during the said period; and
(d) whether Government is aware or have received any reports of instances of diversion of Rice and such foodgrains stipulated for Ethanol production, if so, details thereof?

(a) the total quantity of ethanol consumed for blending with petrol by oil refineries and marketing companies during the last twenty-four months till June, 2026;
(b) the process of scrutiny of the quality of ethanol prior to blending and the parameters checked therein; and
(c) whether any batch of ethanol has been rejected on account of quality concerns during the said period and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether any order, advisory or standard operating procedure has been issued by Government for upgrading the storage infrastructure at retail outlets to store ethanol-blended petrol and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government has conducted or commissioned any study on the effect of ethanol-blended petrol on storage tanks and dispensing infrastructure at fuel stations, including any chemical or physical changes to their surfaces and if so, the findings thereof; and
(c) the details of the studies carried out to scientifically validate ethanol blending programme with respect to its impact on storage infrastructure and on vehicles not compliant with such blending?

(a) the increase in the number of passengers trains originating from the State of Madhya Pradesh during each of the last three years;
(b) whether the augmentation of coaches and the introduction of additional trains have kept pace with the said increase in passenger demand; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor and the steps taken to address the shortfall?

(a) the number of new trains sanctioned with their originating stations in the State of Madhya Pradesh during the last one year, along with the details thereof;
(b) the number of new stoppages provided at railway stations in the State during the said period; and
(c) the criteria adopted for the introduction of new trains and the provision of new stoppages in the State?

(a) the number of officers of various Central Civil Services (other than AIS) recruited through CSE of UPSC serving on deputation or assignments outside their parent service during the last five years;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any review to assess relevance of certain services, such as postal and telecommunication services, in view of adoption of technology;
(c) whether any review of sanctioned cadre strength, like IRS, has been undertaken on account of technological changes and extent of officers remaining on deputation; and
(d) whether Government proposes to review such services and cadre strength, reorganizing redundant services and creating new ones and, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the extent of forest land diverted for non-forest use in the State of Madhya Pradesh during the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the change in the country's forest cover as recorded in the latest assessment as compared with the preceding assessments;
(c) whether the forests in the central region of the country, including Madhya Pradesh, have recorded one of the highest declines in forest cover during this period and if so, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps taken for afforestation and the amount spent for compensatory afforestation during the last five years, State-wise?

(a) whether the Ministry is aware that the Delhi Dehradun Expressway has developed cracks and potholes within few months of its inauguration;
(b) the details of the guarantee of life and condition as mentioned in the project tender;
(c) details of the actions been taken by the Ministry against the project execution agency and the steps being taken for resolution; and
(d) the number of agencies been blacklisted or penalised by the Ministry during the last three years for poor quality work execution or other tender violations?

(a) whether complaints regarding financial misappropriation or irregularities in the procurement or empanelment processes under the CGHS have been received, if so, the action taken thereon and the number of convictions secured;
(b) whether a mechanism exists for CGHS beneficiaries to lodge complaints regarding denial of admission or delay or dilution of services by empanelled hospitals, delayed reimbursement, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of such complaints received during the last three years and the action taken thereon; and
(d) whether any helpline or grievance redressal facility exists for beneficiaries/pensioners facing denial of services at the time of admission, and if so, the details thereof

(a) the total amount of ‘haircut’, being the difference between the admitted claims of creditors and the amount actually realised, borne by financial creditors under the corporate insolvency resolution process during each of the last five years, year-wise;
(b) the average percentage of such haircut borne by creditors in the cases resolved during the said period; and
(c) the share of the said haircut borne by scheduled commercial banks?

(a) whether Government proposes to increase ethanol blending beyond the present 20 per cent, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether any data-backed study has been carried out on the impact of E20 fuel on the performance, efficiency and life of vehicles not compliant with E20 specifications, details thereof;
(c) total quantity and value of ethanol blended with petrol during each of the last three years up to June, 2026, details of the companies from which it was procured and the company-wise payments made during the said period; and
(d) whether the availability of non-blended or lower-blend petrol has been mandated at select fuel stations?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the rising incidents of fraud related to Unified Payments Interface (UPI) transactions reported across the country;
(b) the number of complaints received and the total amount involved in UPI related frauds during the last three years, year-wise;
(c) whether Government has undertaken any assessment regarding the reluctance of certain vendors and small merchants to accept UPI payments, despite the rapid expansion of digital payment systems in the country; and
(d) the steps taken or proposed to strengthen security safeguards in digital payment platforms and to promote wider acceptance of UPI transactions among merchants and consumers?

(a) the total capacity of Strategic Petroleum Reserves (SPR) currently available in the country and the quantity of crude oil presently stored therein;
(b) whether Government has undertaken any recent assessment of India’s increasing dependence on crude oil imports and the potential risks posed to energy security in the event of global geopolitical conflicts or disruptions in key maritime trade routes;
(c) percentage of India’s total crude oil consumption that can presently be supported through existing strategic reserves in case of supply disruptions; and
(d) whether Government proposes to expand strategic petroleum reserve capacity and diversify sources of crude imports?
